Package: IRTsimrel
Title: Reliability-Targeted Simulation for Item Response Data
Version: 0.3.0
Authors@R: 
    person("JoonHo", "Lee", 
           email = "jlee296@ua.edu", 
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0009-0006-4019-8703"))
Description: Provides tools for reliability-targeted simulation studies in
    unidimensional Item Response Theory (IRT), including Rasch, two-parameter
    logistic, and D = 1 three-parameter logistic models. Implements
    topology-aware Empirical Quadrature Calibration (EQC) for fixed forms and
    Stochastic Approximation Calibration (SAC) for fixed-form or
    item-superpopulation targets. Functions generate latent ability
    distributions and item parameters from parametric, hierarchical, custom,
    and optional external Item Response Warehouse (IRW) sources, simulate
    response data with provenance, and provide TAM-based validation for
    supported Rasch and two-parameter logistic workflows.
